# Desktop build-time configuration. electron-vite reads this package's .env
# files at build time; MAIN_VITE_* values are compiled into the main process.
#
# Provider OAuth ("Connect with X" for accounts stored locally on the desktop).
# Optional, per plugin: the button appears for a local account only when the
# plugin declares a desktop client and its public client id is set here. These
# are public clients (PKCE, no secret) registered with the redirect URI
# http://127.0.0.1:43118/oauth/callback (or localhost, per the plugin's
# declaration). OpenRouter and CircleCI need no id; server-only providers
# (GitHub, Bitbucket, Netlify, PlanetScale, Supabase, Vercel, Convex) have none and are connected through cloud mode instead.
# PostHog's id is the URL of the website's /oauth/posthog-desktop.json.
# Uncomment to enable:
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_CLOUDFLARE_CLIENT_ID=<cloudflare-desktop-oauth-client-id>
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_CLOUDINARY_CLIENT_ID=<cloudinary-desktop-oauth-client-id>
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_HUGGINGFACE_CLIENT_ID=<huggingface-desktop-oauth-client-id>
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_PAGERDUTY_CLIENT_ID=<pagerduty-desktop-oauth-client-id>
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_POSTHOG_CLIENT_ID=<posthog-desktop-oauth-client-id>
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_RAILWAY_CLIENT_ID=<railway-desktop-oauth-client-id>
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_RESEND_CLIENT_ID=<resend-desktop-oauth-client-id>
# MAIN_VITE_PROVIDER_OAUTH_SENTRY_CLIENT_ID=<sentry-desktop-oauth-client-id>
